_span":1,"start_col_offset_idx":6,"start_row_offset_idx":7,"text":"0.231 "}]},"footnotes":[],"label":"table","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":227.27593994140625,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":83.19391632080078,"r":529.0352172851562,"t":361.6917724609375},"charspan":[0,0],"page_no":1}],"references":[],"self_ref":"#/tables/0"}],"texts":[{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_header","orig":"29","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":792.9881573478787,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":493.31873248,"r":505.32512627999995,"t":802.7786273599999},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/0","text":"29"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"application sets respectively. In particular, employing a reduced set of templates for template selection leads to an average area reduction of over 27%.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":736.3484901078787,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":90.0,"r":508.4615639200001,"t":766.8387277999999},"charspan":[0,153],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"application sets respectively. In particular, employing a reduced set of templates for template selection leads to an average area reduction of over 27%."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Finally,  Table  3  reports  on  the  efficiency  that  is  obtained  when  the  reduced  set  of templates and the full set of templates are used for template selection. The efficiency is  calculated  as  shown  in  (8),  where ESCS is  the  Effective  Software  Cycle  Savings which  accounts  for  the  hardware  execution  delay  of  the  custom  instructions pi ( TC(pi) ), where i = 1, … , n ,  and is calculated as shown in (9). TC(pi) is  obtained by calculating the number of clusters in the critical path of the custom instructions. For example, TC of the custom instruction in Figure 4(a) is 2. Note that we have assumed that  the  delay  of  each  cluster  is  equivalent  to  two  software  clock  cycle  executions. This  is  a  reasonable  assumption  as  the  FPGA  logic  can  generally  execute  at  a significantly higher clock frequency than a commercially available soft processor core which is implemented on the same fabric [55].","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":487.95089366787874,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":89.99879876000003,"r":508.64668612000037,"t":704.7394247599998},"charspan":[0,952],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"Finally,  Table  3  reports  on  the  efficiency  that  is  obtained  when  the  reduced  set  of templates and the full set of templates are used for template selection. The efficiency is  calculated  as  shown  in  (8),  where ESCS is  the  Effective  Software  Cycle  Savings which  accounts  for  the  hardware  execution  delay  of  the  custom  instructions pi ( TC(pi) ), where i = 1, … , n ,  and is calculated as shown in (9). TC(pi) is  obtained by calculating the number of clusters in the critical path of the custom instructions. For example, TC of the custom instruction in Figure 4(a) is 2. Note that we have assumed that  the  delay  of  each  cluster  is  equivalent  to  two  software  clock  cycle  executions. This  is  a  reasonable  assumption  as  the  FPGA  logic  can  generally  execute  at  a significantly higher clock frequency than a commercially available soft processor core which is implemented on the same fabric [55]."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"K A ESCS Efficiency =","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":429.32996438787876,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":238.79993744,"r":328.20462691999995,"t":455.92097703999997},"charspan":[0,21],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"∑ = ⋅ -× = n i i C i SW i p T p T p F ESCS 1 )) ( 2 ) ( ( ) (","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":389.3795435,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":191.58075659999997,"r":360.07396560000007,"t":415.756356},"charspan":[0,61],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"RFU (8) (9)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":400.52996438787875,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.80030396,"r":386.61912964,"t":448.42043448},"charspan":[0,11],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Table 3: Comparing the efficiency when reduced set and full set of templates are used for template selection","parent":{"$ref":"#/tables/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":187.4701967078788,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":91.38,"r":506.95738668000024,"t":217.96043439999994},"charspan":[0,108],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"Table 3: Comparing the efficiency when reduced set and full set of templates are used for template selection"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"It can be observed in Table 3 that the efficiency of the proposed method is higher than the  case  when  the  full  set  of  templates  is  used  in  a  number  of  application  domains (with  comparable  results  in  the  remaining  domains).  In  particular,  the  average efficiency gain when a reduced set of templates is used is over 25%.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":77.97116450787871,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":89.99977524000002,"r":508.4385156000001,"t":149.8609375599999},"charspan":[0,343],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"It can be observed in Table 3 that the efficiency of the proposed method is higher than the  case  when  the  full  set  of  templates  is  used  in  a  number  of  application  domains (with  comparable  results  in  the  remaining  domains).  In  particular,  the  average efficiency gain when a reduced set of templates is used is over 25%."}],"version":"1.10.0"}